hout exposing credentials or making live requests at query time.\nSolution: Added a versioned, repository-scoped issue evidence store with atomic imports, integrity validation, and workspace-workspace binding. The system:\nIntroduces issues CLI commands (configure, import, status, link, operation, disconnect) and 6 MCP tools for agents to submit evidence without remote calls.\nImplements a local state file that stores issue snapshots, pagination cursors, import progress per project, and work links.\nValidates all records on load (UUID formats, URL schemes, availability markers, timestamp presence) and rejects state corruption.\nSupports resumable imports with run and batch UUIDs, marking incomplete or failed fetch attempts as limitations rather than deleting cached data.\nIntegrates issue citations into retrieval results alongside existing fact and history sources via MCP.\nAdds issue-aware briefs that include workspace and project scope, with paginated evidence delivery (8 KiB pages).\nPublishes a host-neutral workflow spec (docs/linear-workflow.md) explaining import constraints, evidence capture, write authorization, and offline-first retrieval.\nIssue text remains untrusted external evidence; embedded instructions do not authorize Brain tools or the agent host. All mutations operate under the existing Brain write lock, ensuring atomic publication of state changes.", "etag": "W/\"2026-09-17T13:34:32.212187Z\""}}}}
