ory, making these files invisible to the team they were intended for, with no error or warning to alert the user.\nAdditionally, the distill timeout value was hardcoded, making it impossible for users with slow local models or large sessions to adjust the processing timeout.\nSolution:\nAdded a nested repository detection mechanism that identifies when initialization runs inside a git repository nested within another. The OuterRepo function walks the directory hierarchy to find parent repositories and returns the outer one. When detected and no explicit --repo flag is provided, the initialization command now emits a clear warning message that names both repository paths and suggests running the command against the project root instead of the clone.\nAlso made the per-chunk agent timeout configurable via a new --timeout flag on the distill command, allowing users to customize the timeout for their model performance and session size characteristics. The documentation explains the trade-off between timeout and --max-chunk-bytes for different scenarios.", "etag": "W/\"2026-10-01T20:24:17.249742Z\""}}}}
