eVersionId": null, "clientId": "7de422309ccc5f0e97e40078ba1ab82d", "clientIdHash": "2599bae46bc7da47d04f3226a09660c4529102eabef04539a3d3b2409b610995", "createdAt": "2026-10-05T22:04:52.963Z", "updatedAt": "2026-10-05T22:04:52.963Z", "location": {"id": "01M471JAV3YANJDCBS3JED7ZTS", "reviewCommentId": "01M471JAV3WZSRN4HK7SM1EBHD", "codeVersionId": "01M471FN6HXF6P34MW1W9R4K1P", "granularity": "line", "filePath": "internal/cli/semantic.go", "startLine": 2908, "startColumn": null, "endLine": null, "endColumn": null, "selectedText": "\t\t}", "nearbyText": null, "language": null}, "discussionId": "01M471JAV3RA1KZZXHAQ0SKW40"}, {"id": "01M471JATTR2Y868TRX0XP5T1S", "trailId": "01M3ZWMXZHE138HA8W9WK5SYZX", "repositoryId": "01KWZ6252FA5XEMQJYDQ5ZX6RQ", "reviewId": "01M471JATQVFJH2AQM6D98CGAF", "codeVersionId": "01M471FN6HXF6P34MW1W9R4K1P", "actorId": "agent:trail-review", "title": null, "body": "The `stampSemanticHeaderFromLocalGit` function stamps provenance without verifying it was stable across the index run at the point of stamping. While `verifySemanticHeadStable` is called later in `semantic.go:690`, the header is stamped earlier in `semantic_stream.go:159` during stream scanning. If HEAD moves between stamping and verification, the stamped value becomes stale but validation only happens afterwards. Consider moving the verification check immediately before stamping, or re-verifying the commit/tree values at stamp time.", "severity": "medium", "confidence": 0.85, "status": "open", "statusReason": null, "staleOutcome": "current", "staleCheckedAt": null, "staleCheckedCodeVersionId": null, "clientId": "41020eebfa59678a941585ad7e3a449d", "clientIdHash": "af45d34392168640f1df194e463f042949589bbc4b7d64b96205e5cece64cf8a", "createdAt": "2026-10-05T22:04:52.954Z", "updatedAt": "2026-10-05T22:04:52.954Z", "location": {"id": "01M471JATT73A2E2GEK8S1M8GD", "reviewCommentId": "01M471JATTR2Y868TRX0XP5T1S", "codeVersionId": "01M471FN6HXF6P34MW1W9R4K1P", "granularity": "line", "filePath": "internal/cli/semantic_stream.go", "startLine": 159, "startColumn": null, "endLine": null, "endColumn": null, "selectedText": "\t\tres.stampedHeader = stampSemanticHeaderFromLocalGit(&header, cfg.commit, cfg.tree)", "nearbyText": null, "language": null}, "discussionId": "01M471JATTGPP5ZSTNS5HFMTG9"}], "has_more": false, "trail": {"id": "01M3ZWMXZHE138HA8W9WK5SYZX", "number": 246, "branch": "fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows", "originalBranch": "fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows", "base": "fix/retrieval-output-correctness", "title": "fix(safety): stop brain colliding with concurrent git, stalling on a dirty tree, and ignoring local models", "status": "open", "phase": "reviewing", "author": {"id": "01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771", "login": "suhaanthayyil"}, "assignees": ["suhaanthayyil"], "priority": "none", "type": "task", "createdAt": "2026-10-03T03:24:14.193Z", "updatedAt": "2026-10-05T22:04:52.963Z", "unresolvedCount": 2, "bodyDocument": {"textSnapshot": "Now I have enough context. Let me create the summary:\nProblem: Three concurrent safety and usability issues:\nIndexing deadlock on dirty worktrees \u2014 When uncommitted edits existed, the watcher asked Brain to rebuild the index every tick, but runSemanticIndex refused each request with no --worktree flag. This refusal was treated as a failure, aborting the whole tick and leaving the cursor unmoved. The watcher made zero progress for the entire duration the tree stayed dirty (issue #327).\nCommand-line length overflow on Windows \u2014 The entire brain distill command with --agent claude-code failed on every Windows machine with \"The command line is too long\" because the ~7.5 KiB rendered distillation prompt was passed as an argv element. Windows npm-installed claude.cmd and codex.cmd shims route through cmd.exe, which has a hard 8191-character limit (issue #322).\nTranscripts sent to cloud when local model available \u2014 When a user installed ollama (a local LLM) to keep session transcripts off third-party servers, the system either did no distillation or silently sent transcripts to codex/claude-code instead, because ollama was absent from agent selection logic and thus never preferred (issue #328).\nSolution:\nRemoved the unconditional dirty-worktree rebuild requirement from semanticRefreshNeeded() \u2014 dirtiness is redundant since the index describes HEAD and HEAD has not moved. The watch loop now distinguishes a dirty-worktree refusal from real failures and continues instead of aborting the tick.\nRefactored distill agent command building to keep the system prompt off argv. distillAgentCommandArgs() now appends the prompt behind a marker (distillAgentPromptMarker) instead of as a positional argument. prepareAgentExec() extracts it and stages it either as a temp file with --system-prompt-file (claude-code) or composes it into stdin (codex), keeping the command line under cmd.exe's budget.\nReordered agent detection to prefer ollama before cloud CLIs. defaultRefreshAgent() now checks for ollama first, making local models the default when available. Watch defaults distillAgent to \"auto\" instead of hardcoded \"codex\", resolving to the preferred agent at runtime.\nAdded regression tests for all three fixes: dirty-worktree stalling, Windows command-line length, git refresh behavior with stat-dirty files, and local-model preference.", "etag": "W/\"2026-10-03T03:24:56.231704Z\""}}}}
